<div id="S1.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 1.7</span></span><span id="S1.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Corollary <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem11" title="Corollary 6.11. ‣ 6.2. Asymptotic log-concavity ‣ 6. Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.11</span></a>)<span id="S1.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="S1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}&amp;\left(\mathscr{P}_{n,k}^{n-j}\right)^{2}\geq\left(\mathscr{P}_{n,k}^{n-j-1}\right)\cdot\left(\mathscr{P}_{n,k}^{n-j+1}\right)~\text{ and}\\
&amp;\left(\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}^{n-j}\right)^{2}\geq\left(\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}^{n-j-1}\right)\cdot\left(\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}^{n-j+1}\right)\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and</mtext></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}&amp;\left(\mathscr{P}_{n,k}^{n-j}\right)^{2}\geq\left(\mathscr{P}_{n,k}^{n-j-1}\right)\cdot\left(\mathscr{P}_{n,k}^{n-j+1}\right)~\text{ and}\\
&amp;\left(\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}^{n-j}\right)^{2}\geq\left(\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}^{n-j-1}\right)\cdot\left(\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}^{n-j+1}\right)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for any sufficiently large <math id="S1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 1.5 (Theorem ). ‣ 1.4. Asymptotic formulas and log-concavity ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.5</span></a> and Corollary <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem6" title="Corollary 1.6 (Corollary ). ‣ 1.4. Asymptotic formulas and log-concavity ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.6</span></a> generalize the results by Aluffi-Chen-Marcolli in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite> on
the Betti numbers of <math id="S1.SS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which correspond to the case where <math id="S1.SS4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0</annotation></semantics></math> (Remark <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem7" title="Remark 6.7 (Leading coefficients). ‣ 6.1. Asymptotic formulas ‣ 6. Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.7</span></a>).
It remains open whether the ultra log-concavity for <math id="S1.SS4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0</annotation></semantics></math> in Corollary <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem6" title="Corollary 1.6 (Corollary ). ‣ 1.4. Asymptotic formulas and log-concavity ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.6</span></a> holds for all <math id="S1.SS4.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas explicit formulas for the Betti numbers have recently been obtained in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">All cohomology groups in this paper are singular cohomology with rational coefficients and all <math id="S1.SS4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-representations are defined over <math id="S1.SS4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℚ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
