<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2. </span>Two-dimensional log-concavity</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A sequence <math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> of nonnegative real numbers is called <em id="S2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">log-concave</em> if</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}^{2}\geq a_{k-1}a_{k+1}\quad\text{for all }k." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}^{2}\geq a_{k-1}a_{k+1}\quad\text{for all }k.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The log-concavity extends to arbitrary real sequences by taking the sequence of absolute values <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a_{k}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a_{k}|</annotation></semantics></math>.
A nonnegative finite sequence <math id="S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{a_{k}\right\}_{k=0}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{a_{k}\right\}_{k=0}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="S2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ultra log-concave</em> if the normalized sequence</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{\frac{a_{k}}{\binom{n}{k}}\right\}_{0\leq k\leq n}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\frac{a_{k}}{\binom{n}{k}}\right\}_{0\leq k\leq n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">is log-concave.
In what follows, any property defined in terms of log-concavity is similarly extended to define the corresponding notion of ultra log-concavity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A polynomial <math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(m)=\sum_{k=0}^{n}a_{k}m^{k}\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(m)=\sum_{k=0}^{n}a_{k}m^{k}\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m]</annotation></semantics></math> with nonnegative coefficients is said to be <em id="S2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">log-concave</em> if the sequence <math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave. We say <math id="S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(m)</annotation></semantics></math> has <em id="S2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">no internal zeros</em> if there do not exist integers <math id="S2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;j&lt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;j&lt;k</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we generalize the notion of log-concavity to a two-dimensional array <math id="S2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A^{j}_{k}\}_{0\leq j,k\leq N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A^{j}_{k}\}_{0\leq j,k\leq N}</annotation></semantics></math> of nonnegative real numbers or to a bivariate polynomial</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(m,t)=\sum_{k\geq 0}\sum_{j\geq 0}A_{k}^{j}m^{j}t^{k}~\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m,t]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(m,t)=\sum_{k\geq 0}\sum_{j\geq 0}A_{k}^{j}m^{j}t^{k}~\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m,t].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}(m)=\sum_{j\geq 0}A_{k}^{j}m^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}(m)=\sum_{j\geq 0}A_{k}^{j}m^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{j}(t)=\sum_{k\geq 0}A_{k}^{j}t^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{j}(t)=\sum_{k\geq 0}A_{k}^{j}t^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> so that we have</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(m,t)=\sum_{k}A_{k}(m)t^{k}=\sum_{j}A^{j}(t)m^{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(m,t)=\sum_{k}A_{k}(m)t^{k}=\sum_{j}A^{j}(t)m^{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">From the matrix <math id="S2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A^{j}_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A^{j}_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, there are many ways to extract a sequence of numbers and define log-concavity. In this paper, we will consider the following natural choices.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(m,t)=\sum_{j,k\geq 0}A_{k}^{j}m^{j}t^{k}~\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(m,t)=\sum_{j,k\geq 0}A_{k}^{j}m^{j}t^{k}~\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m,t]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0},m_{0}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0},m_{0}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ol id="S2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">length log-concave in degree <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></em> if <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}(m)=\sum_{j\geq 0}A_{k}^{j}m^{j}\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}(m)=\sum_{j\geq 0}A_{k}^{j}m^{j}\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m]</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">length log-concave at <math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></em> if
<math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(m,t_{0})\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(m,t_{0})\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m]</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">degree log-concave in length <math id="S2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math></em> if <math id="S2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{j}(t)=\sum_{k\geq 0}A_{k}^{j}t^{k}\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{j}(t)=\sum_{k\geq 0}A_{k}^{j}t^{k}\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[t]</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="S2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">degree log-concave at <math id="S2.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=m_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=m_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></em>
if
<math id="S2.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(m_{0},t)\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(m_{0},t)\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[t]</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This definition extends to arbitrary bivariate real polynomials <math id="S2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(m,t)\in\mathbb{R}[m,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(m,t)\in\mathbb{R}[m,t]</annotation></semantics></math> by taking the absolute values <math id="S2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A^{j}_{k}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A^{j}_{k}|</annotation></semantics></math> of the coefficients.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We call <math id="S2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> the <em id="S2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">degree</em> variable and <math id="S2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> the <em id="S2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">length</em> variable since
we will see below that if <math id="S2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> comes from the cohomology <math id="S2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{*}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{*}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> of a space <math id="S2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> acted on by the symmetric group <math id="S2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the exponent of the variable <math id="S2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the length of a partition and the exponent of the variable <math id="S2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> keeps track of the cohomological degree.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 2.2</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In §<a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4. Characteristic polynomial of an 𝕊_𝑛-representation ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, we will associate a polynomial <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)\in\mathbb{Q}[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)\in\mathbb{Q}[m]</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>
to each finite dimensional <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> by applying the principal specialization map in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, §7.8]</cite> to the Frobenius characteristic of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem10" title="Lemma 3.10. ‣ 3.4. Characteristic polynomial of an 𝕊_𝑛-representation ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a>, the coefficient of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n!}\mathrm{dim}\,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>dim</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n!}\mathrm{dim}\,V</annotation></semantics></math> and the dimension of the invariant part equals</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dim}\,V^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}=\mathscr{S}_{V}(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>dim</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dim}\,V^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}=\mathscr{S}_{V}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">When the <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\bigoplus_{k\geq 0}V_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\bigoplus_{k\geq 0}V_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is graded, we associate the polynomial</p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}(m,t)=\sum_{k}\mathscr{S}_{V_{k}}(m)t^{k}\in\mathbb{Q}[m,t]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}(m,t)=\sum_{k}\mathscr{S}_{V_{k}}(m)t^{k}\in\mathbb{Q}[m,t].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In this case, the degree log-concavity in length <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to the
log-concavity of the sequence <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathrm{dim}\,V_{k}\}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>dim</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathrm{dim}\,V_{k}\}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>
while the degree log-concavity at <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to the
log-concavity of the sequence <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathrm{dim}\,V_{k}^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}\}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>dim</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathrm{dim}\,V_{k}^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}\}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>
of the dimensions of the invariant parts.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, when</p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\bigoplus_{k\geq 0}H^{2k}(\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\bigoplus_{k\geq 0}H^{2k}(\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">is the cohomology of the moduli space <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-pointed stable curves of genus <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, we note that
the degree log-concavity in length <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>
is the log-concavity of the Betti numbers proved asymptotically by Aluffi-Chen-Marcolli <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, while
the degree log-concavity at <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>
is the log-concavity of the invariant part proved asymptotically in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>.
Below we will find more log-concavity results about the graded <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{*}(\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{*}(\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n})</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of the log-concavities in Definition <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 2.1. ‣ 2. Two-dimensional log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 2.3</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In §<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, we will associate a polynomial <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)\in\mathbb{Q}[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)\in\mathbb{Q}[m]</annotation></semantics></math> of degree at most <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> to each symmetric function <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in\Lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in\Lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> by the principal specialization map in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, §7.8]</cite>.
When <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\sum_{k\geq 0}F_{k}t^{k}\in\Lambda_{n}[t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\sum_{k\geq 0}F_{k}t^{k}\in\Lambda_{n}[t]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{k}\in\Lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{k}\in\Lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we associate <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{F}(m,t)=\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathscr{S}_{F_{k}}(m)t^{k}\in\mathbb{Q}[m,t]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{F}(m,t)=\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathscr{S}_{F_{k}}(m)t^{k}\in\mathbb{Q}[m,t].</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given a graph <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the chromatic quasisymmetric function <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{cqsf}_{\Gamma}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖼𝗊𝗌𝖿</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{cqsf}_{\Gamma}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> defined in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>.
When <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is the graph associated to a Hessenberg function in §<a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3. Hessenberg varieties ‣ 4. Characteristic polynomials of varieties and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\mathsf{cqsf}_{\Gamma}(t)\in\Lambda_{n}[t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖼𝗊𝗌𝖿</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\mathsf{cqsf}_{\Gamma}(t)\in\Lambda_{n}[t]</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{F}(m,1)=\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{csf}_{\Gamma}}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>𝖼𝗌𝖿</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{F}(m,1)=\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{csf}_{\Gamma}}(m)</annotation></semantics></math> is the usual chromatic polynomial <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{X}_{\Gamma}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒳</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{X}_{\Gamma}(m)</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, the length log-concavity at <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{F}(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{F}(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the log-concavity of the chromatic polynomial of the graph <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> which is a special case of the celebrated theorem of June Huh in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We end this section with the following well known results which will be used below.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.4</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a><span id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, Proposition 2]</span></cite><span id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
If <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f,g\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f,g\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m]</annotation></semantics></math> are log-concave with no internal zeros, then so is <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="fg\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">fg\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.5</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a><span id="S2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, Theorem 2]</span></cite><span id="S2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
If <math id="S2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}[m]</annotation></semantics></math> has only real roots, then <math id="S2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3. </span>Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we investigate useful properties of the principal specialization map or the <em id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Stanley map</em> in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, §7.8]</cite>
which associates a polynomial <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)\in\mathbb{Q}[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)\in\mathbb{Q}[m]</annotation></semantics></math> to each symmetric function <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in\Lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in\Lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.
A remarkable feature of the Stanley map</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}:\Lambda_{n}\longrightarrow\mathbb{Q}[m],\quad F\mapsto\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}:\Lambda_{n}\longrightarrow\mathbb{Q}[m],\quad F\mapsto\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is that it sends the plethysm operation on <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> to the composition on <math id="S3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}[m]</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 3.2. ‣ 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>).
In fact, this property uniquely determines the Stanley map (Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>).
Since the plethysm operation usually causes computational difficulties, the Stanley map levitates computational burdens while keeping core information, just like the characteristic polynomial of a matrix.
In this vein, we call <math id="S3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)\in\mathbb{Q}[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)\in\mathbb{Q}[m]</annotation></semantics></math> the <em id="S3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">characteristic polynomial</em> of <math id="S3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> (Definition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 3.1. ‣ 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>).
When the symmetric function is the chromatic symmetric function of a graph defined by Stanley in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>, its characteristic polynomial is the usual chromatic polynomial of Birkhoff’s, which is log-concave by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By applying the Stanley map to the Frobenius characteristic <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ch}(V)\in\Lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ch</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ch}(V)\in\Lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of an <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain a polynomial
<math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)\in\mathbb{Q}[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)\in\mathbb{Q}[m]</annotation></semantics></math> which we call the <em id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">characteristic polynomial</em> of <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>. When
<math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\bigoplus_{k\geq 0}V_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\bigoplus_{k\geq 0}V_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is graded, its characteristic polynomial</p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}(m,t)=\sum_{k}\mathscr{S}_{V_{k}}(m)t^{k}\in\mathbb{Q}[m,t]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}(m,t)=\sum_{k}\mathscr{S}_{V_{k}}(m)t^{k}\in\mathbb{Q}[m,t]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">allows us to consider the two-dimensional log-concavities in Definition <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 2.1. ‣ 2. Two-dimensional log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.
In the subsequent sections, we will find interesting examples where the log-concavities hold.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1. </span>Symmetric functions and plethysm</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we set up our notation on symmetric functions and recall basic facts about plethysm.
For further details and undefined terms, we refer the reader to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Lambda=\lim_{\longleftarrow}\mathbb{Q}\llbracket x_{1},\cdots,x_{n}\rrbracket^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟵</mo></munder><mi>ℚ</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda=\lim_{\longleftarrow}\mathbb{Q}\llbracket x_{1},\cdots,x_{n}\rrbracket^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">be the power series ring of symmetric functions in variables <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2},\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2},\cdots</annotation></semantics></math>, with <em id="S3.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">rational</em> coefficients.
Let <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{n}\subset\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{n}\subset\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> denote the subspace of elements of degree <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda=\prod_{n\geq 0}\Lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda=\prod_{n\geq 0}\Lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For an integer <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, let</p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{p}_{n}=\sum_{i\geq 1}x_{i}^{n},\quad\mathsf{h}_{n}=\sum_{1\leq i_{1}\leq\cdots\leq i_{n}}x_{i_{1}}\cdots x_{i_{n}}\mathsf{e}_{n}=\sum_{1\leq i_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;i_{n}}x_{i_{1}}\cdots x_{i_{n}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗉</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>𝗁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mi>𝖾</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{p}_{n}=\sum_{i\geq 1}x_{i}^{n},\quad\mathsf{h}_{n}=\sum_{1\leq i_{1}\leq\cdots\leq i_{n}}x_{i_{1}}\cdots x_{i_{n}}\mathsf{e}_{n}=\sum_{1\leq i_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;i_{n}}x_{i_{1}}\cdots x_{i_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">be the <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th power sum symmetric function,
homogeneous symmetric function and
elementary symmetric function, respectively.
For convenience, we set <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{p}_{0}=\mathsf{h}_{0}=\mathsf{e}_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝖾</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{p}_{0}=\mathsf{h}_{0}=\mathsf{e}_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a partition <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\cdots,\lambda_{\ell})\vdash n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\cdots,\lambda_{\ell})\vdash n</annotation></semantics></math>,
let</p>
<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}=\mathsf{p}_{\lambda_{1}}\cdots\mathsf{p}_{\lambda_{\ell}},\quad\mathsf{h}_{\lambda}=\mathsf{h}_{\lambda_{1}}\cdots\mathsf{h}_{\lambda_{\ell}}\mathsf{e}_{\lambda}=\mathsf{e}_{\lambda_{1}}\cdots\mathsf{e}_{\lambda_{\ell}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗉</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝗉</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>𝗉</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>𝗁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝗁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>𝗁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mi>𝖾</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖾</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>𝖾</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}=\mathsf{p}_{\lambda_{1}}\cdots\mathsf{p}_{\lambda_{\ell}},\quad\mathsf{h}_{\lambda}=\mathsf{h}_{\lambda_{1}}\cdots\mathsf{h}_{\lambda_{\ell}}\mathsf{e}_{\lambda}=\mathsf{e}_{\lambda_{1}}\cdots\mathsf{e}_{\lambda_{\ell}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Then each of <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}\}_{\lambda\vdash n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}\}_{\lambda\vdash n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathsf{h}_{\lambda}\}_{\lambda\vdash n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathsf{h}_{\lambda}\}_{\lambda\vdash n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathsf{e}_{\lambda}\}_{\lambda\vdash n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝖾</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathsf{e}_{\lambda}\}_{\lambda\vdash n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a basis for <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For a partition <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\lambda}=\prod_{i\geq 1}i^{m_{i}}m_{i}!" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\lambda}=\prod_{i\geq 1}i^{m_{i}}m_{i}!</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of parts of <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> equal to <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. We let <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define a symmetric bilinear form <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle-,-\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle-,-\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathsf{p}_{\lambda},\mathsf{p}_{\mu}\rangle=z_{\lambda}\delta_{\lambda\mu}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathsf{p}_{\lambda},\mathsf{p}_{\mu}\rangle=z_{\lambda}\delta_{\lambda\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">so that <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is an orthogonal basis.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">There is a ring homomorphism <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega:\Lambda\to\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega:\Lambda\to\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> defined by</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega(\mathsf{p}_{n})=(-1)^{n-1}\mathsf{p}_{n}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega(\mathsf{p}_{n})=(-1)^{n-1}\mathsf{p}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Clearly <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> is an isometric involution and satisfies <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega(\mathsf{e}_{\lambda})=\mathsf{h}_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖾</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega(\mathsf{e}_{\lambda})=\mathsf{h}_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\vdash n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\vdash n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">On <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, there is an associative binary operation <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\circ" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∘</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\circ</annotation></semantics></math>, called the <em id="S3.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">plethysm</em>,
which is uniquely determined by the following properties: for <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F,G,H\in\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F,G,H\in\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\circ\mathsf{p}_{n}=\mathsf{p}_{n}\circ F=F(x_{1}^{n},x_{2}^{n},\cdots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\circ\mathsf{p}_{n}=\mathsf{p}_{n}\circ F=F(x_{1}^{n},x_{2}^{n},\cdots)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F+G)\circ H=F\circ H+G\circ H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F+G)\circ H=F\circ H+G\circ H</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(FG)\circ H=(F\circ H)(G\circ H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(FG)\circ H=(F\circ H)(G\circ H)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{p}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{p}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the two-sided identity with respect to <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\circ" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∘</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\circ</annotation></semantics></math> by (1). This naturally extends to such an operation <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\circ" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∘</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\circ</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\llbracket t\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\llbracket t\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying (2) and (3) with <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\llbracket t\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\llbracket t\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> as well as</p>
<ol id="S3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S3.I2.ix1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S3.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I2.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\circ\mathsf{p}_{n}=\mathsf{p}_{n}\circ F=F(t^{n},x_{1}^{n},x_{2}^{n},\cdots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\circ\mathsf{p}_{n}=\mathsf{p}_{n}\circ F=F(t^{n},x_{1}^{n},x_{2}^{n},\cdots)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.I2.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.I2.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\circ F=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\circ F=t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\llbracket t\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\llbracket t\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> with no constant term, the <em id="S3.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">plethystic exponential</em> of <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is defined to be</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Exp(F)=\sum_{r\geq 0}\mathsf{h}_{r}\circ F=\exp\sum_{r\geq 1}\frac{1}{r}\mathsf{p}_{r}\circ F" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Exp(F)=\sum_{r\geq 0}\mathsf{h}_{r}\circ F=\exp\sum_{r\geq 1}\frac{1}{r}\mathsf{p}_{r}\circ F</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where the second equality holds since <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{r\geq 0}\mathsf{h}_{r}=\exp\sum_{r\geq 1}\frac{1}{r}\mathsf{p}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>𝗁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mi>𝗉</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{r\geq 0}\mathsf{h}_{r}=\exp\sum_{r\geq 1}\frac{1}{r}\mathsf{p}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2. </span>Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we introduce the Stanley map and the characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions.
We further characterize the Stanley map as the only algebra homomorphism that converts plethysm to composition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in\Lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in\Lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be a symmetric function of degree <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}c_{\lambda}\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}c_{\lambda}\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>. The <em id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">characteristic polynomial</em> of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is defined to be</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}c_{\lambda}m^{\ell(\lambda)}\ \ \in\mathbb{Q}[m]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}c_{\lambda}m^{\ell(\lambda)}\ \ \in\mathbb{Q}[m]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the length of a partition <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. For
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\sum_{k}F_{k}t^{k}\in\Lambda_{n}[t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\sum_{k}F_{k}t^{k}\in\Lambda_{n}[t]</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{k}\in\Lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{k}\in\Lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and a formal variable <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,
we define</p>
<table id="S3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{F}(m,t)=\sum_{k}\mathscr{S}_{F_{k}}(m)t^{k}\ \ \in\mathbb{Q}[m,t]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{F}(m,t)=\sum_{k}\mathscr{S}_{F_{k}}(m)t^{k}\ \ \in\mathbb{Q}[m,t].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the degree of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is at most <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. It is easy to see that for any positive integer <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{F}(m_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{F}(m_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained from <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> by the substitution (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1.1. Chromatic polynomial and characteristic polynomial ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>).
By (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.1. Symmetric functions and plethysm ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>), (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In Definition 3.1. ‣ 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>) can be also written as</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}z_{\lambda}^{-1}\langle F,\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}\rangle m^{\ell(\lambda)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}z_{\lambda}^{-1}\langle F,\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}\rangle m^{\ell(\lambda)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By Definition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 3.1. ‣ 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, we have the map</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}:\Lambda_{n}\longrightarrow\mathbb{Q}[m],\quad F\mapsto\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}:\Lambda_{n}\longrightarrow\mathbb{Q}[m],\quad F\mapsto\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and its extension</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathscr{S}}:\Lambda\longrightarrow\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q\rrbracket,\quad(F\in\Lambda_{n})\mapsto\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)q^{n}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathscr{S}}:\Lambda\longrightarrow\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q\rrbracket,\quad(F\in\Lambda_{n})\mapsto\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)q^{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is a formal variable recording the degree <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>) is a <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℚ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra homomorphism, called the <em id="S3.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">principal specialization</em> in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, §7.8]</cite>,
or the <em id="S3.SS2.p3.3.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Stanley map</em>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">A remarkable feature of (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>) is that they convert plethysm to composition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in\Lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in\Lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in\Lambda_{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in\Lambda_{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,n^{\prime}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,n^{\prime}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{F\circ G}(m)=(\mathscr{S}_{F}\circ\mathscr{S}_{G})(m)=\mathscr{S}_{F}(\mathscr{S}_{G}(m))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{F\circ G}(m)=(\mathscr{S}_{F}\circ\mathscr{S}_{G})(m)=\mathscr{S}_{F}(\mathscr{S}_{G}(m)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{p}_{r}\circ G}=\mathscr{S}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{p}_{r}\circ G}=\mathscr{S}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in\Lambda_{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in\Lambda_{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, if <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}a_{\lambda}\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}a_{\lambda}\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}a_{\lambda}m^{\ell(\lambda)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{F}(m)=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}a_{\lambda}m^{\ell(\lambda)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{F\circ G}(m)=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}a_{\lambda}\prod_{i=1}^{\ell(\lambda)}\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{p}_{\lambda_{i}}\circ G}(m)=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}a_{\lambda}(\mathscr{S}_{G}(m))^{\ell(\lambda)}=\mathscr{S}_{F}(\mathscr{S}_{G}(m))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{F\circ G}(m)=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}a_{\lambda}\prod_{i=1}^{\ell(\lambda)}\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{p}_{\lambda_{i}}\circ G}(m)=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}a_{\lambda}(\mathscr{S}_{G}(m))^{\ell(\lambda)}=\mathscr{S}_{F}(\mathscr{S}_{G}(m))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">for any <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in\Lambda_{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in\Lambda_{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\cdots,\lambda_{\ell(\lambda)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\cdots,\lambda_{\ell(\lambda)})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">If we extend the composition <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f\circ g)(m)=f(g(m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f\circ g)(m)=f(g(m))</annotation></semantics></math> to an operation on <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\sum_{i}f_{i}(m)q^{i}\right)\circ\left(\sum_{j}g_{j}(m)q^{j}\right)=\sum_{i,j}f_{i}(g_{j}(m))q^{ij}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\sum_{i}f_{i}(m)q^{i}\right)\circ\left(\sum_{j}g_{j}(m)q^{j}\right)=\sum_{i,j}f_{i}(g_{j}(m))q^{ij},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 3.2. ‣ 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> is equivalent to</p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{F\circ G}=\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{F}\circ\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{G}\in\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q\rrbracket\quad\text{for }F,G\in\Lambda." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{F\circ G}=\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{F}\circ\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{G}\in\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q\rrbracket\quad\text{for }F,G\in\Lambda.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p">Conversely, (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In Proposition 3.2. ‣ 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.8</span></a>) or (<a href="#S3.E10" title="In 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a>) determines <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathscr{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathscr{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> and thus <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The map <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathscr{S}}:\Lambda\to\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathscr{S}}:\Lambda\to\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℚ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra homomorphism that sends <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}[m]q^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}[m]q^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and satisfies (<a href="#S3.E10" title="In 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be another such homomorphism and let <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}^{\prime}:\Lambda_{n}\to\mathbb{Q}[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}^{\prime}:\Lambda_{n}\to\mathbb{Q}[m]</annotation></semantics></math> be defined by <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}_{F}=\mathscr{S}^{\prime}_{F}(m)q^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}_{F}=\mathscr{S}^{\prime}_{F}(m)q^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in\Lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in\Lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{p}_{n}\circ a=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{p}_{n}\circ a=a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}^{\prime}_{a}=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}^{\prime}_{a}=a</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\Lambda_{0}=\mathbb{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\Lambda_{0}=\mathbb{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}_{\mathsf{p}_{n}}(a)=\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}_{\mathsf{p}_{n}}(\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}_{a}(m))=\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}_{\mathsf{p}_{n}\circ a}(m)=\mathscr{S}^{\prime}_{a}(m)q^{n}=aq^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}_{\mathsf{p}_{n}}(a)=\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}_{\mathsf{p}_{n}}(\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}_{a}(m))=\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}_{\mathsf{p}_{n}\circ a}(m)=\mathscr{S}^{\prime}_{a}(m)q^{n}=aq^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}^{\prime}_{\mathsf{p}_{n}}(m)=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}^{\prime}_{\mathsf{p}_{n}}(m)=m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}_{\mathsf{p}_{n}}=mq^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}_{\mathsf{p}_{n}}=mq^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. The uniqueness follows from this because <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathscr{S}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℚ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra homomorphism.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">All these extend to a graded version with a new variable <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mathscr{S}}:\Lambda\llbracket t\rrbracket\longrightarrow\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket,\quad\mathsf{p}_{n}t^{k}\mapsto mq^{n}t^{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathscr{S}}:\Lambda\llbracket t\rrbracket\longrightarrow\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket,\quad\mathsf{p}_{n}t^{k}\mapsto mq^{n}t^{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p">By abuse of notation, we denote this map also by <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathscr{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathscr{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If we extend the composition to an operation <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q\rrbracket\times\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket\to\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q\rrbracket\times\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket\to\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="S3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\sum_{i}f_{i}(m)q^{i}\right)\circ\left(\sum_{j,k}g_{jk}(m)q^{j}t^{k}\right)=\sum_{i,j,k}f_{i}(g_{jk}(m))q^{ij}t^{ik}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\sum_{i}f_{i}(m)q^{i}\right)\circ\left(\sum_{j,k}g_{jk}(m)q^{j}t^{k}\right)=\sum_{i,j,k}f_{i}(g_{jk}(m))q^{ij}t^{ik},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p">Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 3.2. ‣ 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> upgrades to</p>
<table id="S3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{F\circ G}=\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{F}\circ\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{G}\in\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket\quad\text{for }F\in\Lambda,~G\in\Lambda\llbracket t\rrbracket." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{F\circ G}=\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{F}\circ\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{G}\in\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket\quad\text{for }F\in\Lambda,~G\in\Lambda\llbracket t\rrbracket.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.4</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The map (<a href="#S3.E11" title="In 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.11</span></a>) is the unique <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℚ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra homomorphism
that sends <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{n}\llbracket t\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{n}\llbracket t\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket t\rrbracket q^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket t\rrbracket q^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and satisfied (<a href="#S3.E13" title="In 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.13</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is basically the same as that for Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Finally we observe that <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies a duality with respect to the involution (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.1. Symmetric functions and plethysm ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>) on <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> (cf. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>, Exercise 24]</cite>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.5</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-duality)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in\Lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in\Lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{\omega F}(m)=(-1)^{n}\mathscr{S}_{F}(-m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{\omega F}(m)=(-1)^{n}\mathscr{S}_{F}(-m)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">This follows immediately from <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}=(-1)^{n-\ell(\lambda)}\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}=(-1)^{n-\ell(\lambda)}\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\vdash n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\vdash n</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3. </span>Plethysm on polynomials</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For convenience, we introduce the plethysm operation on polynomials as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.6</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in\Lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in\Lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the plethysm</p>
<table id="S3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="F\circ(-):\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket\longrightarrow\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket,\quad F\circ\left(f(m)q^{i}t^{j}\right)=\mathscr{S}_{F}(f(m))q^{ni}t^{nj}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\circ(-):\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket\longrightarrow\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket,\quad F\circ\left(f(m)q^{i}t^{j}\right)=\mathscr{S}_{F}(f(m))q^{ni}t^{nj}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, we extend it linearly.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It is straightforward to check that <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\circ(-)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\circ(-)</annotation></semantics></math> is uniquely characterized by the following properties: for <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f\in\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F,G\in\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F,G\in\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<ol id="S3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{p}_{n}\circ f=f^{[n]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{p}_{n}\circ f=f^{[n]}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F+G)\circ f=F\circ f+G\circ f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F+G)\circ f=F\circ f+G\circ f</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(FG)\circ f=(F\circ f)(G\circ f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(FG)\circ f=(F\circ f)(G\circ f)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where
<math id="S3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{[n]}(m,q,t)=f(m,q^{n},t^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{[n]}(m,q,t)=f(m,q^{n},t^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{p}_{n}\circ(-)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{p}_{n}\circ(-)</annotation></semantics></math> leaves <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> unchanged, while <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> are raised to the <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th power. If <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}c_{\lambda}\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}c_{\lambda}\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\circ f=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}c_{\lambda}f^{[\lambda]}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\circ f=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}c_{\lambda}f^{[\lambda]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where we write <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f^{[\lambda]}:=f^{[\lambda_{1}]}\cdots f^{[\lambda_{\ell}]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{[\lambda]}:=f^{[\lambda_{1}]}\cdots f^{[\lambda_{\ell}]}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\cdots,\lambda_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\cdots,\lambda_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f\in\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathbb{Q}[m]\llbracket q,t\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> with no constant term, as in (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1. Symmetric functions and plethysm ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>), we define the <em id="S3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">plethystic exponential</em> of <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> to be</p>
<table id="S3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Exp(f)=\sum_{r\geq 0}\mathsf{h}_{r}\circ f=\exp\sum_{r\geq 1}\frac{1}{r}\mathsf{p}_{r}\circ f=\exp\sum_{r\geq 1}\frac{1}{r}f^{[r]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></mfrac><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Exp(f)=\sum_{r\geq 0}\mathsf{h}_{r}\circ f=\exp\sum_{r\geq 1}\frac{1}{r}\mathsf{p}_{r}\circ f=\exp\sum_{r\geq 1}\frac{1}{r}f^{[r]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 3.7</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Monomial)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For integers <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,j,n,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,j,n,k</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j,n,k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j,n,k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="S3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\Exp(am^{j}q^{n}t^{k})&amp;=\exp\sum_{r\geq 1}\frac{1}{r}am^{j}q^{rn}t^{rk}\\
&amp;=\exp(-am^{j}\mathrm{log}(1-q^{n}t^{k}))=(1-q^{n}t^{k})^{-am^{j}}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\Exp(am^{j}q^{n}t^{k})&amp;=\exp\sum_{r\geq 1}\frac{1}{r}am^{j}q^{rn}t^{rk}\\
&amp;=\exp(-am^{j}\mathrm{log}(1-q^{n}t^{k}))=(1-q^{n}t^{k})^{-am^{j}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">provided <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n,k)\neq(0,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n,k)\neq(0,0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 3.8</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Alternative description of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Exp(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Exp(f)</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that</p>
<table id="S3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{h}_{n}=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}z_{\lambda}^{-1}\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{h}_{n}=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}z_{\lambda}^{-1}\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for any <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Exp(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Exp(f)</annotation></semantics></math> can also be written as</p>
<table id="S3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Exp(f)=\sum_{r\geq 0}\mathsf{h}_{r}\circ f=\sum_{\lambda\in\mathrm{Par}}z_{\lambda}^{-1}f^{[\lambda]}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Par</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Exp(f)=\sum_{r\geq 0}\mathsf{h}_{r}\circ f=\sum_{\lambda\in\mathrm{Par}}z_{\lambda}^{-1}f^{[\lambda]},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Par}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Par</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Par}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of partitions of nonnegative integers and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{[0]}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{[0]}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4. </span>Characteristic polynomial of an <math id="S3.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we define the characteristic polynomial of an <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> by applying the Stanley map <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}</annotation></semantics></math> to the Frobenius characteristic of <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{n}=\mathrm{Rep}(\mathbb{S}_{n})_{\mathbb{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Rep</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{n}=\mathrm{Rep}(\mathbb{S}_{n})_{\mathbb{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℚ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>-vector space spanned by irreducible <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-representations and let <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}=\mathbb{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}=\mathbb{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\prod_{n\geq 0}R_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\prod_{n\geq 0}R_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the ring of virtual representations of the symmetric groups whose ring structure is given by</p>
<table id="S3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V.W=\mathrm{Ind}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}\times\mathbb{S}_{m}}^{\mathbb{S}_{n+m}}V\otimes W" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Ind</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V.W=\mathrm{Ind}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}\times\mathbb{S}_{m}}^{\mathbb{S}_{n+m}}V\otimes W</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">for an <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> and an <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then it is well-known that the Frobenius characteristic map</p>
<table id="S3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{ch}:R\,\smash{\mathop{\longrightarrow}\limits^{\cong}}\,\Lambda,\quad\mathrm{ch}(V)=\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(V)=\frac{1}{n!}\sum_{\sigma\in\mathbb{S}_{n}}\mathrm{Tr}_{V}(\sigma)\mathsf{p}_{\sigma}\ \ \text{ for }V\in R_{n}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ch</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>R</mi><mover><mo lspace="0.448em" stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mo>≅</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>ch</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>Tr</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mtext> for </mtext><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ch}:R\,\smash{\mathop{\longrightarrow}\limits^{\cong}}\,\Lambda,\quad\mathrm{ch}(V)=\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(V)=\frac{1}{n!}\sum_{\sigma\in\mathbb{S}_{n}}\mathrm{Tr}_{V}(\sigma)\mathsf{p}_{\sigma}\ \ \text{ for }V\in R_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">is a ring isomorphism where
<math id="S3.SS4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{p}_{\sigma}:=\mathsf{p}_{\lambda(\sigma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{p}_{\sigma}:=\mathsf{p}_{\lambda(\sigma)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\sigma)\vdash n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\sigma)\vdash n</annotation></semantics></math> is
the cycle partition of <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. This sends the Specht module <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> to the Schur function <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{s}_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗌</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{s}_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the length of the partition <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.9</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <em id="S3.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">characteristic polynomial</em> of an <math id="S3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>
is</p>
<table id="S3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)=\mathscr{S}_{\mathrm{ch}(V)}(m)=\frac{1}{n!}\sum_{\sigma\in\mathbb{S}_{n}}\mathrm{Tr}_{V}(\sigma)m^{\ell(\sigma)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>ch</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>Tr</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)=\mathscr{S}_{\mathrm{ch}(V)}(m)=\frac{1}{n!}\sum_{\sigma\in\mathbb{S}_{n}}\mathrm{Tr}_{V}(\sigma)m^{\ell(\sigma)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\bigoplus_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}V_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\bigoplus_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}V_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is a graded <math id="S3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-module,
we let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}(m,t)=\sum_{k}\mathscr{S}_{V_{k}}(m)t^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}(m,t)=\sum_{k}\mathscr{S}_{V_{k}}(m)t^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The coefficients of <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> keep essential information about <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.10</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in R_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in R_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="S3.Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation.</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The coefficient of </span><math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in </span><math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is </span><math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n!}\mathrm{dim}\,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>dim</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n!}\mathrm{dim}\,V</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The value </span><math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}(1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of </span><math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> at </span><math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the dimension of the invariant subspace </span><math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1)^{n}\cdot\mathscr{S}_{V}(-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{n}\cdot\mathscr{S}_{V}(-1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the multiplicity of the sign representation </span><math id="S3.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{sgn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗌𝗀𝗇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{sgn}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in the decomposition of </span><math id="S3.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> into irreducible representations.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">(1) is a direct consequence of the facts that <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\sigma)=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\sigma)=n</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Tr}_{V}(e)=\mathrm{dim}\,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Tr</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>dim</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Tr}_{V}(e)=\mathrm{dim}\,V</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">(2) follows from (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>) and the identity <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(\mathbbm{1})=\mathsf{h}_{n}=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}z_{\lambda}^{-1}\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(\mathbbm{1})=\mathsf{h}_{n}=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}z_{\lambda}^{-1}\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbbm{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>𝟙</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbbm{1}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the trivial representation. Indeed,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}(1)=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}z_{\lambda}^{-1}\langle\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(V),\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}\rangle=\langle\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(V),\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(\mathbbm{1})\rangle=\langle V,\mathbbm{1}\rangle=\mathrm{dim}\,V^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟙</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>dim</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}(1)=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}z_{\lambda}^{-1}\langle\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(V),\mathsf{p}_{\lambda}\rangle=\langle\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(V),\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(\mathbbm{1})\rangle=\langle V,\mathbbm{1}\rangle=\mathrm{dim}\,V^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">(3) follows from (2) and Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5 (𝜔-duality). ‣ 3.2. Characteristic polynomial of a symmetric function ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>, since <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(V)=\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(V\otimes\mathsf{sgn})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝗌𝗀𝗇</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(V)=\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(V\otimes\mathsf{sgn})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5. </span>First examples</h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we work out examples of the characteristic polynomials of <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 3.11</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, Example I.2.1]</cite>

When <math id="S3.Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\mathbbm{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\mathbbm{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the trivial representation, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(\mathbbm{1})=\mathsf{h}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(\mathbbm{1})=\mathsf{h}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. By (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1.1. Chromatic polynomial and characteristic polynomial ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="S3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{h}_{n}}(m)=\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right):=\binom{n+m-1}{n}=\frac{m(m+1)\cdots(m+n-1)}{n!}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{h}_{n}}(m)=\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right):=\binom{n+m-1}{n}=\frac{m(m+1)\cdots(m+n-1)}{n!}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem11.p1.2" class="ltx_p">since <math id="S3.Thmtheorem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{h}_{n}=\sum_{1\leq i_{1}\leq\cdots\leq i_{n}}x_{i_{1}}\cdots x_{i_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{h}_{n}=\sum_{1\leq i_{1}\leq\cdots\leq i_{n}}x_{i_{1}}\cdots x_{i_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Similarly, when <math id="S3.Thmtheorem11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\mathsf{sgn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝗌𝗀𝗇</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\mathsf{sgn}</annotation></semantics></math> is the sign representation, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(\mathsf{sgn})=\mathsf{e}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗌𝗀𝗇</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝖾</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(\mathsf{sgn})=\mathsf{e}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="S3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{e}_{n}}=\binom{m}{n}=\frac{m(m-1)\cdots(m-n+1)}{n!}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>𝖾</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{e}_{n}}=\binom{m}{n}=\frac{m(m-1)\cdots(m-n+1)}{n!}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem11.p1.3" class="ltx_p">since <math id="S3.Thmtheorem11.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{e}_{n}=\sum_{1\leq i_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;i_{n}}x_{i_{1}}\cdots x_{i_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖾</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{e}_{n}=\sum_{1\leq i_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;i_{n}}x_{i_{1}}\cdots x_{i_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 3.12</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Permutation modules)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <em id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">permutation <math id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-module</em>
associated to a partition <math id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\cdots,\lambda_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\cdots,\lambda_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the induced representation</p>
<table id="S3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\lambda}:=\mathrm{Ind}^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}_{\mathbb{S}_{\lambda}}\mathbbm{1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Ind</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟙</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\lambda}:=\mathrm{Ind}^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}_{\mathbb{S}_{\lambda}}\mathbbm{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.2" class="ltx_p">of the trivial representation of the Young subgroup <math id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{\lambda}=\mathbb{S}_{\lambda_{1}}\times\cdots\times\mathbb{S}_{\lambda_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{\lambda}=\mathbb{S}_{\lambda_{1}}\times\cdots\times\mathbb{S}_{\lambda_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Its dimension is <math id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{n!}/{\lambda!}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{n!}/{\lambda!}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda!=\lambda_{1}!\cdots\lambda_{\ell}!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>!</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda!=\lambda_{1}!\cdots\lambda_{\ell}!</annotation></semantics></math> and we have</p>
<table id="S3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(M^{\lambda})=\mathsf{h}_{\lambda}=\mathsf{h}_{\lambda_{1}}\cdots\mathsf{h}_{\lambda_{\ell}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(M^{\lambda})=\mathsf{h}_{\lambda}=\mathsf{h}_{\lambda_{1}}\cdots\mathsf{h}_{\lambda_{\ell}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Hence by multiplicativity,</p>
<table id="S3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathscr{S}_{M^{\lambda}}(m)&amp;=\prod_{i=1}^{\ell}\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{\lambda_i}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)=\frac{1}{\lambda!}m^{\lambda^{t}_{1}}(m+1)^{\lambda^{t}_{2}}\cdots(m+{\lambda_{1}}-1)^{\lambda^{t}_{\lambda_{1}}}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo></mpadded><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0em;" width="0em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mpadded><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathscr{S}_{M^{\lambda}}(m)&amp;=\prod_{i=1}^{\ell}\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{\lambda_i}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)=\frac{1}{\lambda!}m^{\lambda^{t}_{1}}(m+1)^{\lambda^{t}_{2}}\cdots(m+{\lambda_{1}}-1)^{\lambda^{t}_{\lambda_{1}}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>
denotes the dual partition of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> with parts <math id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{t}_{1}\geq\cdots\geq\lambda^{t}_{\lambda_{1}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{t}_{1}\geq\cdots\geq\lambda^{t}_{\lambda_{1}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{t}_{1}=\ell(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{t}_{1}=\ell(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is the length of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and (<a href="#S3.E17" title="In Example 3.12 (Permutation modules). ‣ 3.5. First examples ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.17</span></a>) is divisible by <math id="S3.Thmtheorem12.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\ell(\lambda)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\ell(\lambda)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">From this, we deduce the following.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.13</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="S3.Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation with
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}b_{\lambda}M^{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\sum_{\lambda\vdash n}b_{\lambda}M^{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{(n)}/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{(n)}/n</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is equal to the coefficient of </span><math id="S3.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I5.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in </span><math id="S3.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I5.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{(1^{n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{(1^{n})}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is equal to </span><math id="S3.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1)^{n}\cdot\mathscr{S}_{V}(-1)=\mathrm{dim}~(V\otimes\mathsf{sgn})^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>dim</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝗌𝗀𝗇</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{n}\cdot\mathscr{S}_{V}(-1)=\mathrm{dim}~(V\otimes\mathsf{sgn})^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#S3.E17" title="In Example 3.12 (Permutation modules). ‣ 3.5. First examples ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.17</span></a>), we find that, for <math id="S3.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\cdots,\lambda_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\cdots,\lambda_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I6" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I6.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S3.I6.ix1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S3.I6.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I6.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I6.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{M^{\lambda}}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{M^{\lambda}}(m)</annotation></semantics></math> is divisible by <math id="S3.I6.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and the coefficient of <math id="S3.I6.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.I6.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{1}/{(\lambda_{1}\cdots\lambda_{n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{1}/{(\lambda_{1}\cdots\lambda_{n})}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I6.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S3.I6.ix2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S3.I6.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I6.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I6.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{M^{\lambda}}(-1)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{M^{\lambda}}(-1)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="S3.I6.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=(1^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=(1^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I6.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{M^{(1^{n})}}(-1)=(-1)^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{M^{(1^{n})}}(-1)=(-1)^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S3.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The statements (1) and (2) follow immediately from <math id="S3.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 3.14</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Permutation representations)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <em id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">permutation representation</em> of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a representation of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> that admits an <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant basis. It is called <em id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">transitive</em> if an (or equivalently any) <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant basis consists of a single orbit. Every permutation representation of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> decomposes as a direct sum of transitive ones and every transitive permutation representation is the induced representation</p>
<table id="S3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{H}:=\mathrm{Ind}^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}_{H}\mathbbm{1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Ind</mi><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟙</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{H}:=\mathrm{Ind}^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}_{H}\mathbbm{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.2" class="ltx_p">of the trivial representation of some subgroup <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, any <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant basis of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is isomorphic to <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}/H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}/H</annotation></semantics></math> as an <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-set. In particular,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(U_{H})&amp;=\frac{1}{n!}\sum_{\sigma\in\mathbb{S}_{n}}\left\lvert(\mathbb{S}_{n}/H)^{\sigma}\right\rvert\cdot\mathsf{p}_{\sigma}\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{n!}\sum_{\sigma\in\mathbb{S}_{n}}\left\lvert\{\tau H\in\mathbb{S}_{n}/H:\sigma\in\tau H\tau^{-1}\}\right\rvert\cdot\mathsf{p}_{\sigma}\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{n!}\sum_{\tau H\in\mathbb{S}_{n}/H}\sum_{\sigma\in\tau H\tau^{-1}}\mathsf{p}_{\sigma}\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{n!}\sum_{\tau H\in\mathbb{S}_{n}/H}\sum_{\sigma^{\prime}\in H}\mathsf{p}_{\sigma^{\prime}}=\frac{1}{\lvert H\rvert}\sum_{\sigma^{\prime}\in H}\mathsf{p}_{\sigma^{\prime}}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>σ</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(U_{H})&amp;=\frac{1}{n!}\sum_{\sigma\in\mathbb{S}_{n}}\left\lvert(\mathbb{S}_{n}/H)^{\sigma}\right\rvert\cdot\mathsf{p}_{\sigma}\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{n!}\sum_{\sigma\in\mathbb{S}_{n}}\left\lvert\{\tau H\in\mathbb{S}_{n}/H:\sigma\in\tau H\tau^{-1}\}\right\rvert\cdot\mathsf{p}_{\sigma}\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{n!}\sum_{\tau H\in\mathbb{S}_{n}/H}\sum_{\sigma\in\tau H\tau^{-1}}\mathsf{p}_{\sigma}\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{n!}\sum_{\tau H\in\mathbb{S}_{n}/H}\sum_{\sigma^{\prime}\in H}\mathsf{p}_{\sigma^{\prime}}=\frac{1}{\lvert H\rvert}\sum_{\sigma^{\prime}\in H}\mathsf{p}_{\sigma^{\prime}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the first equality holds since the <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> acts on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> as a permutation on the basis <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}/H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}/H</annotation></semantics></math> and the second equality holds since <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\tau H=\tau H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\tau H=\tau H</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\tau H\tau^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\tau H\tau^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The fourth equality follows from setting <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=\tau\sigma^{\prime}\tau^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=\tau\sigma^{\prime}\tau^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{p}_{\sigma}=\mathsf{p}_{\sigma^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝗉</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{p}_{\sigma}=\mathsf{p}_{\sigma^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the third and the last equalities are immediate.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Consequently, the characteristic polynomial of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{U_{H}}(m)=\frac{1}{\lvert H\rvert}\sum_{\sigma\in H}m^{\ell(\sigma)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{U_{H}}(m)=\frac{1}{\lvert H\rvert}\sum_{\sigma\in H}m^{\ell(\sigma)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p2.2" class="ltx_p">In other words, the coefficient of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{U_{H}}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{U_{H}}(m)</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of permutations contained in <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> that have precisely <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> orbits in <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[n]:=\{1,\cdots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[n]:=\{1,\cdots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>, divided by <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert H\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert H\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We note that for a positive integer <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the value <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{U_{H}}(m_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{U_{H}}(m_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the number of ways to color the elements in <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[n]</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> colors, where two colorings are considered equivalent if they belong to the same <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>-orbit under the natural <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>-action on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[n]</annotation></semantics></math> (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, Corollary 7.24.6]</cite>).</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 3.15</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem15.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a permutation representation <math id="S3.Thmtheorem15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>
of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> always has nonnegative coefficients.
On the other hand,
it may have internal zeros in its coefficients. For example, for <math id="S3.Thmtheorem15.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=\langle(1,2,3)\rangle\subset\mathbb{S}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=\langle(1,2,3)\rangle\subset\mathbb{S}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem15.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{U_{H}}=\frac{1}{3}(m^{3}+m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{U_{H}}=\frac{1}{3}(m^{3}+m)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 3.16</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Specht module)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\cdots,\lambda_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\cdots,\lambda_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> be a partition of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}\geq\cdots\geq\lambda_{\ell}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}\geq\cdots\geq\lambda_{\ell}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq\ell</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{s}_{\lambda}}(m)=\prod_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq m}\left(1+\frac{\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j}}{j-i}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>𝗌</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{s}_{\lambda}}(m)=\prod_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq m}\left(1+\frac{\lambda_{i}-\lambda_{j}}{j-i}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In particular, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{s}_{\lambda}}(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>𝗌</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{s}_{\lambda}}(n)</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the dimension of the irreducible <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="GL_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">GL_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> with the highest weight <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, by the Weyl dimension formula. See <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, (7.106) or (A.2.4)]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 3.17</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that an <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is spanned by <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\lambda)\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\lambda)\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.
In this case, the representation <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is completely determined by its characteristic polynomial <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)</annotation></semantics></math>. To see this, write</p>
<table id="S3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\sum_{0\leq j\leq\frac{n}{2}}c_{j}M^{(n-j,j)},\quad c_{j}\in\mathbb{Z}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\sum_{0\leq j\leq\frac{n}{2}}c_{j}M^{(n-j,j)},\quad c_{j}\in\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so that</p>
<table id="S3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)=\sum_{1\leq j\leq\frac{n}{2}}c_{j}\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{h}_{(n-j,j)}}(m),\quad\text{where }~\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{h}_{(n-j,j)}}=\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n-j}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{j}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}(m)=\sum_{1\leq j\leq\frac{n}{2}}c_{j}\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{h}_{(n-j,j)}}(m),\quad\text{where }~\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{h}_{(n-j,j)}}=\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n-j}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{j}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Letting <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\lfloor\frac{n}{2}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\lfloor\frac{n}{2}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="S3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{ij}:=\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{h}_{(n-j,j)}}(i-n)=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{ if }i&gt;j\\
(-1)^{n}\binom{n-i}{n-j}\binom{n-i}{j}&amp;\text{ if }i\leq j\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{ij}:=\mathscr{S}_{\mathsf{h}_{(n-j,j)}}(i-n)=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{ if }i&gt;j\\
(-1)^{n}\binom{n-i}{n-j}\binom{n-i}{j}&amp;\text{ if }i\leq j\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.4" class="ltx_p">for <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq i\leq r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq i\leq r</annotation></semantics></math>,
since <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\kern-3.00003pt\big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{i-n}{n-j}\big)\kern-3.00003pt\big)=(-1)^{n-j}\binom{n-i}{n-j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\kern-3.00003pt\big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{i-n}{n-j}\big)\kern-3.00003pt\big)=(-1)^{n-j}\binom{n-i}{n-j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\kern-3.00003pt\big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{i-n}{j}\big)\kern-3.00003pt\big)=(-1)^{j}\binom{n-i}{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\kern-3.00003pt\big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{i-n}{j}\big)\kern-3.00003pt\big)=(-1)^{j}\binom{n-i}{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The upper triangular matrix <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=(B_{ij})_{0\leq i,j\leq r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=(B_{ij})_{0\leq i,j\leq r}</annotation></semantics></math> has nonzero determinant <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1)^{n(r+1)}\prod_{i=0}^{r}\binom{n-i}{i}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{n(r+1)}\prod_{i=0}^{r}\binom{n-i}{i}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{V}(i-n)=\sum_{j=0}^{r}B_{ij}c_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{V}(i-n)=\sum_{j=0}^{r}B_{ij}c_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq i\leq r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq i\leq r</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are determined by the matrix multiplication</p>
<table id="S3.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c_{0},\cdots,c_{r})^{t}=B^{-1}\cdot(\mathscr{S}_{V}(-n),\cdots,\mathscr{S}_{V}(r-n))^{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c_{0},\cdots,c_{r})^{t}=B^{-1}\cdot(\mathscr{S}_{V}(-n),\cdots,\mathscr{S}_{V}(r-n))^{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4. </span>Characteristic polynomials of varieties and log-concavity</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present examples derived from geometry. Let <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth projective pure-dimensional variety with no odd degree cohomology, i.e. <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{2k+1}(Z)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{2k+1}(Z)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that <math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is equipped with an <math id="S4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-action, or more generally, <math id="S4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{2k}(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{2k}(Z)</annotation></semantics></math> is equipped with an <math id="S4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-action for every <math id="S4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the characteristic polynomial of the induced graded <math id="S4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{*}(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{*}(Z)</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="S4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{Z}(m,t)=\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathscr{S}_{\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}H^{2k}(Z)}(m)t^{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{Z}(m,t)=\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathscr{S}_{\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}H^{2k}(Z)}(m)t^{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We call this <em id="S4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">the characteristic polynomial of <math id="S4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math></em>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{Z}(m,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{Z}(m,1)</annotation></semantics></math> is the characteristic polynomial of the ungraded <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(Z)=\bigoplus_{k}H^{2k}(Z)\in R_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(Z)=\bigoplus_{k}H^{2k}(Z)\in R_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{Z}(1,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{Z}(1,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the Poincaré polynomial of the invariant part <math id="S4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{*}(Z)^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{*}(Z)^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is isomorphic to <math id="S4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{*}(Z/\mathbb{S}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{*}(Z/\mathbb{S}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> when there is an <math id="S4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-action on <math id="S4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1. </span><math id="S4.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-fold products</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth projective variety with no odd cohomology.
Consider the <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-action on the <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-fold product <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X^{n}=X\times\cdots\times X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{n}=X\times\cdots\times X</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> given by permuting the product components. This can be viewed as the space of
ordered <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> points in <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> acted on by an <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-action reordering them.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We compute <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{X^{n}}(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{X^{n}}(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> and explore the four types of log-concavities introduced in Definition <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 2.1. ‣ 2. Two-dimensional log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.
We begin with an example where <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Observe that</p>
<table id="S4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}H^{2k}(X^{n})t^{k}=\mathsf{h}_{n}\circ(\mathsf{h}_{1}+\mathsf{h}_{1}t)=\sum_{k=0}^{n}\mathsf{h}_{n-k}\mathsf{h}_{k}t^{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}H^{2k}(X^{n})t^{k}=\mathsf{h}_{n}\circ(\mathsf{h}_{1}+\mathsf{h}_{1}t)=\sum_{k=0}^{n}\mathsf{h}_{n-k}\mathsf{h}_{k}t^{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Applying the Stanley map <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(m,t)=\sum_{k=0}^{n}\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n-k}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{k}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)t^{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(m,t)=\sum_{k=0}^{n}\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n-k}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{k}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)t^{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In particular, when evaluated at <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>, one gets</p>
<table id="S4.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}&amp;\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(m,1)=\sum_{k=0}^{n}\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n-k}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{k}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)=\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{2m}{n}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big);\\
&amp;\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(1,t)=\sum_{k=0}^{n}t^{k}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0em;" width="0em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0em;" width="0em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0em;" width="0em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}&amp;\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(m,1)=\sum_{k=0}^{n}\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n-k}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{k}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)=\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{2m}{n}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big);\\
&amp;\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(1,t)=\sum_{k=0}^{n}t^{k}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">respectively. By (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Example 4.1. ‣ 4.1. 𝑛-fold products ‣ 4. Characteristic polynomials of varieties and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E2" title="In Example 4.1. ‣ 4.1. 𝑛-fold products ‣ 4. Characteristic polynomials of varieties and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>), we find that</p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is length log-concave in degree <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq k\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq k\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is length log-concave at <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is degree log-concave at <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">respectively, where the first and the second statements follow by Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 2.4. ‣ 2. Two-dimensional log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a> or <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 2.5. ‣ 2. Two-dimensional log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>.
However, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is not degree log-concave in a given length in general. For example, when <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=4</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{4}}(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{4}}(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}(t^{4}+1)m+\frac{1}{24}(11t^{4}+8t^{3}+6t^{2}+8t+11)m^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>24</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}(t^{4}+1)m+\frac{1}{24}(11t^{4}+8t^{3}+6t^{2}+8t+11)m^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{4}(1+2t+2t^{2}+2t^{3}+t^{4})m^{3}+\frac{1}{24}(t^{4}+4t^{3}+6t^{2}+4t+1)m^{4}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>24</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{4}(1+2t+2t^{2}+2t^{3}+t^{4})m^{3}+\frac{1}{24}(t^{4}+4t^{3}+6t^{2}+4t+1)m^{4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">which is not degree log-concave in length 2.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, interestingly, it seems to hold that</p>
<ul id="S4.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{(\mathbb{P}^{1})^{n}}(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is degree log-concave in length <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> whenever the inequalities <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil\mathrm{log}_{2}(n\mathrm{log}_{2}n)\rceil\leq\ell\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil\mathrm{log}_{2}(n\mathrm{log}_{2}n)\rceil\leq\ell\leq n</annotation></semantics></math> are satisfied.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We have checked this for <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 200</annotation></semantics></math> by numerical computation. We also note that the bound <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil\mathrm{log}_{2}(n\mathrm{log}_{2}n)\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil\mathrm{log}_{2}(n\mathrm{log}_{2}n)\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> is not sharp.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For general <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, we can explicitly calculate <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{X^{n}}(m,t)\in\mathbb{Q}[m,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{X^{n}}(m,t)\in\mathbb{Q}[m,t]</annotation></semantics></math>,
and study the log-concavity.
Let <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{X}=\sum_{k=0}^{d}b_{k}t^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{X}=\sum_{k=0}^{d}b_{k}t^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the Poincaré polynomial of <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=\mathrm{dim}\,X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>dim</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=\mathrm{dim}\,X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{k}=\mathrm{dim}\,H^{2k}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>dim</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{k}=\mathrm{dim}\,H^{2k}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We set <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to be a point. Then,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n\geq 0}\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}H^{2k}(X^{n})t^{k}=\Exp(p_{X}\mathsf{h}_{1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n\geq 0}\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}H^{2k}(X^{n})t^{k}=\Exp(p_{X}\mathsf{h}_{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently, the generating series of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{X^{n}}(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{X^{n}}(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="S4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n\geq 0}\mathscr{S}_{X^{n}}(m,t)q^{n}=\prod_{i=0}^{d}\left(1-qt^{i}\right)^{-b_{i}m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n\geq 0}\mathscr{S}_{X^{n}}(m,t)q^{n}=\prod_{i=0}^{d}\left(1-qt^{i}\right)^{-b_{i}m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the Künneth formula and the property of the plethysm by <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{h}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{h}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}H^{2k}(X^{n})t^{k}=\mathsf{h}_{n}\circ\left(\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{1}}H^{2k}(X)t^{k}\right)=\mathsf{h}_{n}\circ(p_{X}\mathsf{h}_{1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}H^{2k}(X^{n})t^{k}=\mathsf{h}_{n}\circ\left(\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{1}}H^{2k}(X)t^{k}\right)=\mathsf{h}_{n}\circ(p_{X}\mathsf{h}_{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, we obtain (<a href="#S4.E3" title="In Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.1. 𝑛-fold products ‣ 4. Characteristic polynomials of varieties and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>) by the definition of plethystic exponential.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The formula (<a href="#S4.E4" title="In Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.1. 𝑛-fold products ‣ 4. Characteristic polynomials of varieties and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>) follows from (<a href="#S4.E3" title="In Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.1. 𝑛-fold products ‣ 4. Characteristic polynomials of varieties and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>), by applying <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{(-)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{(-)}</annotation></semantics></math> since</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{\Exp(p_{X}\mathsf{h}_{1})}&amp;=\exp\sum_{r\geq 1}\frac{1}{r}\mathsf{p}_{r}\circ\widehat{\mathscr{S}}(p_{X}\mathsf{h}_{1})=\exp m\sum_{r\geq 1}\frac{1}{r}\mathsf{p}_{r}\circ(p_{X}q)=\left(\Exp(p_{X}q)\right)^{m}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mi>𝗉</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝗁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mi>m</mi><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mi>𝗉</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>Exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\widehat{\mathscr{S}}_{\Exp(p_{X}\mathsf{h}_{1})}&amp;=\exp\sum_{r\geq 1}\frac{1}{r}\mathsf{p}_{r}\circ\widehat{\mathscr{S}}(p_{X}\mathsf{h}_{1})=\exp m\sum_{r\geq 1}\frac{1}{r}\mathsf{p}_{r}\circ(p_{X}q)=\left(\Exp(p_{X}q)\right)^{m}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is equal to <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{i=0}^{d}(1-qt^{i})^{-b_{i}m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{i=0}^{d}(1-qt^{i})^{-b_{i}m}</annotation></semantics></math> by Example <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Example 3.7 (Monomial). ‣ 3.3. Plethysm on polynomials ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 4.3</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be as above.</span></p>
<ol id="S4.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S4.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">As an element of </span><math id="S4.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}[m][t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}[m][t]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S4.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{X^{n}}(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{X^{n}}(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I3.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is written as</span></p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{X^{n}}(m,t)=\sum_{n_{0}+\cdots+n_{d}=n}\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{b_0m}{n_0}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)\cdots\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{b_dm}{n_d}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)t^{1\cdot n_{1}+\cdots+d\cdot n_{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{X^{n}}(m,t)=\sum_{n_{0}+\cdots+n_{d}=n}\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{b_0m}{n_0}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)\cdots\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{b_dm}{n_d}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)t^{1\cdot n_{1}+\cdots+d\cdot n_{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
