</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem15.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem15.p2.1" class="ltx_p">(2) It is also observed that, regarding Conjecture <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem14" title="Conjecture 5.14. ‣ 5.2. Recursive formulas for characteristic polynomials ‣ 5. Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.14</span></a>(4), <math id="S5.Thmtheorem15.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{P}_{n}(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{P}_{n}(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem15.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}_{n}(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}_{n}(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> are <em id="S5.Thmtheorem15.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> degree log-concave in all lengths in general. For example, since <math id="S5.Thmtheorem15.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{5}=\mathsf{h}_{5}+\mathsf{h}_{4}\mathsf{h}_{1}t+\mathsf{h}_{5}t^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{5}=\mathsf{h}_{5}+\mathsf{h}_{4}\mathsf{h}_{1}t+\mathsf{h}_{5}t^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="S5.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{P}_{5}(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{P}_{5}(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{m^{5}}{120}+\frac{m^{4}}{12}+\frac{7m^{3}}{24}+\frac{5m^{2}}{12}+\frac{m}{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mn>120</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mn>24</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{m^{5}}{120}+\frac{m^{4}}{12}+\frac{7m^{3}}{24}+\frac{5m^{2}}{12}+\frac{m}{5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\left(\frac{m^{5}}{24}+\frac{m^{4}}{4}+\frac{11m^{3}}{24}+\frac{m^{2}}{4}\right)t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mn>24</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mn>24</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\left(\frac{m^{5}}{24}+\frac{m^{4}}{4}+\frac{11m^{3}}{24}+\frac{m^{2}}{4}\right)t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
