<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\left(\frac{m^{5}}{120}+\frac{m^{4}}{12}+\frac{7m^{3}}{24}+\frac{5m^{2}}{12}+\frac{m}{5}\right)t^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mn>120</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mn>24</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\left(\frac{m^{5}}{120}+\frac{m^{4}}{12}+\frac{7m^{3}}{24}+\frac{5m^{2}}{12}+\frac{m}{5}\right)t^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem15.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which is not degree log-concave in length 1 and 2.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem15.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem15.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, when <math id="S5.Thmtheorem15.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=6</annotation></semantics></math>, applying (<a href="#S6.E1" title="In Remark 6.8 (Linear terms). ‣ 6.1. Asymptotic formulas ‣ 6. Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>) yields the sequence</p>
<table id="S5.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathscr{Q}_{6,k}^{1}\}_{k=0}^{4}=\left\{\frac{1}{6},\frac{1}{6},\frac{1}{3},\frac{1}{6},\frac{1}{6}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathscr{Q}_{6,k}^{1}\}_{k=0}^{4}=\left\{\frac{1}{6},\frac{1}{6},\frac{1}{3},\frac{1}{6},\frac{1}{6}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem15.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Hence, <math id="S5.Thmtheorem15.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}_{6}</annotation></semantics></math> is not degree log-concave in length 1. We note that the bound <math id="S5.Thmtheorem15.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}+2</annotation></semantics></math> in Conjecture <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem14" title="Conjecture 5.14. ‣ 5.2. Recursive formulas for characteristic polynomials ‣ 5. Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.14</span></a>(4) is not sharp.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">In §<a href="#S6" title="6. Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we will use Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem11" title="Theorem 5.11. ‣ 5.2. Recursive formulas for characteristic polynomials ‣ 5. Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.11</span></a> and Corollary <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem12" title="Corollary 5.12. ‣ 5.2. Recursive formulas for characteristic polynomials ‣ 5. Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.12</span></a> to deduce asymptotic formulas and asymptotic log-concavities for the characteristic polynomials of <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3. </span>Interpretation as the count of colorings</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we present an interpretation of the characteristic polynomial <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{U_{T}}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{U_{T}}(m)</annotation></semantics></math> of (<a href="#S5.E1" title="In Definition 5.6. ‣ 5.1. Recursive formulas for the representations ‣ 5. Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>) and its chromatic polynomial <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}^{\omega}_{U_{T}}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mi>ω</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}^{\omega}_{U_{T}}(m)</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of colorings, which may be of independent interest.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first recall an inductive decomposition of weighted rooted trees, based on which the recursion in Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem 5.10. ‣ 5.1. Recursive formulas for the representations ‣ 5. Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.10</span></a> was established in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.16</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a><span id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, Lemma 4.4]</span></cite><span id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
Let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\mathscr{T}_{n,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\mathscr{T}_{n,k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the root vertex of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of the inputs attached to <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and the weight given at <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively.
Let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1},\cdots,v_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1},\cdots,v_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> be the non-root vertices of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> adjacent to <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq p</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the weighted rooted subtree of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<ol id="S5.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">its underlying rooted subtree has </span><math id="S5.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I5.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as its root;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(T_{i}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(T_{i}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> consists of </span><math id="S5.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in V(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in V(T)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I5.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that </span><math id="S5.I5.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I5.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S5.I5.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I5.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are connected by a path in </span><math id="S5.I5.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I5.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> which does not pass through </span><math id="S5.I5.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I5.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S5.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the edges (resp. inputs) of </span><math id="S5.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I5.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are precisely those of </span><math id="S5.I5.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I5.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> connecting (resp. attached to) the vertices in </span><math id="S5.I5.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(T_{i}^{\prime})\subset V(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(T_{i}^{\prime})\subset V(T)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I5.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S5.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I5.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the weight function on </span><math id="S5.I5.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(T_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(T_{i})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I5.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the restriction of that of </span><math id="S5.I5.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I5.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}\in\mathscr{T}_{n_{0},k_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}\in\mathscr{T}_{n_{0},k_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the weighted rooted tree with only one vertex. Now let</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{T_{1}^{\prime},\cdots,T_{p}^{\prime}\}=\{T_{1},\cdots,T_{1},\cdots,T_{l},\cdots,T_{l}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{T_{1}^{\prime},\cdots,T_{p}^{\prime}\}=\{T_{1},\cdots,T_{1},\cdots,T_{l},\cdots,T_{l}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are mutually non-isomorphic and there are <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> copies of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume that <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{j}\in\mathscr{T}_{n_{j},k_{j}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{j}\in\mathscr{T}_{n_{j},k_{j}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n_{0}+\sum_{j=1}^{l}r_{j}n_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n_{0}+\sum_{j=1}^{l}r_{j}n_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=k_{0}+\sum_{j=1}^{l}r_{j}k_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=k_{0}+\sum_{j=1}^{l}r_{j}k_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then,</span></p>
<table id="S5.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}U_{T}=\mathsf{h}_{n_{0}}\cdot\prod_{j=1}^{l}\mathsf{h}_{r_{j}}\circ\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}}(U_{T_{j}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>l</mi></munderover><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}U_{T}=\mathsf{h}_{n_{0}}\cdot\prod_{j=1}^{l}\mathsf{h}_{r_{j}}\circ\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}}(U_{T_{j}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Furthermore, by taking the involution <math id="S5.Thmtheorem16.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\omega(\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}U_{T})=\mathsf{e}_{n_{0}}\prod_{r_{j}:\;\mathrm{even}}\mathsf{h}_{r_{j}}\circ\omega(\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}}U_{T_{j}})\prod_{r_{j}:\;\mathrm{odd}}\mathsf{e}_{r_{j}}\circ\omega(\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}}U_{T_{j}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝖾</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mi>even</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></msub><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mi>odd</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝖾</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></msub><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega(\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}U_{T})=\mathsf{e}_{n_{0}}\prod_{r_{j}:\;\mathrm{even}}\mathsf{h}_{r_{j}}\circ\omega(\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}}U_{T_{j}})\prod_{r_{j}:\;\mathrm{odd}}\mathsf{e}_{r_{j}}\circ\omega(\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}}U_{T_{j}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
