<p id="S5.Thmtheorem23.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="S5.Thmtheorem23.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> has only one vertex, namely the root, and all the <math id="S5.Thmtheorem23.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> inputs are attached to the root, as in Example <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem7" title="Example 5.7. ‣ 5.1. Recursive formulas for the representations ‣ 5. Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.7</span></a>. Then,</p>
<table id="S5.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}U_{T}=\mathsf{h}_{n}\quad\text{ so that }\quad\mathscr{S}_{U_{T}}(m)=\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> so that </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}U_{T}=\mathsf{h}_{n}\quad\text{ so that }\quad\mathscr{S}_{U_{T}}(m)=\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
