</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem24" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 5.24</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem24.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem24.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="S5.Thmtheorem24.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> has only two vertices with <math id="S5.Thmtheorem24.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> inputs attached to the root and the remaining <math id="S5.Thmtheorem24.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-a</annotation></semantics></math> inputs attached to the other non-root vertex, as in Example <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem8" title="Example 5.8. ‣ 5.1. Recursive formulas for the representations ‣ 5. Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.8</span></a>. Then,</p>
<table id="S5.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}U_{T}=\mathsf{h}_{a}\mathsf{h}_{n-a}\quad\text{ so that }\quad\mathscr{S}_{U_{T}}(m)=\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{a}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n-a}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> so that </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}U_{T}=\mathsf{h}_{a}\mathsf{h}_{n-a}\quad\text{ so that }\quad\mathscr{S}_{U_{T}}(m)=\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{a}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n-a}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem24.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This counts the number of colorings of the inputs of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem24.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S5.Thmtheorem24.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> colors.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem25" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem25.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 5.25</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem25.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem25.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem25.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="S5.Thmtheorem25.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> be the weighted rooted tree with three vertices, given in Example <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem9" title="Example 5.9. ‣ 5.1. Recursive formulas for the representations ‣ 5. Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.9</span></a>.
Then, <math id="S5.Thmtheorem25.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(U_{T})=\mathsf{h}_{n-2a}\cdot(\mathsf{h}_{2}\circ\mathsf{h}_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ch</mi><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ch}_{\mathbb{S}_{n}}(U_{T})=\mathsf{h}_{n-2a}\cdot(\mathsf{h}_{2}\circ\mathsf{h}_{a})</annotation></semantics></math> so that</p>
<table id="S5.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{U_{T}}(m)=\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n-2a}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{\multiset{m}{a}}{2}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{U_{T}}(m)=\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n-2a}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{\multiset{m}{a}}{2}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem25.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This counts the number of colorings of the inputs of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem25.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S5.Thmtheorem25.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> colors.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem26" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem26.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 5.26</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="S5.Thmtheorem26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-twisted version)<span id="S5.Thmtheorem26.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem26.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem26.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the above examples, one can easily see that taking <math id="S5.Thmtheorem26.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to restricting to proper colorings.
Indeed,</p>
<table id="S5.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}^{\omega}_{\mathsf{h}_{n}}(m)=\binom{m}{n}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>𝗁</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>ω</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}^{\omega}_{\mathsf{h}_{n}}(m)=\binom{m}{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem26.p1.2" class="ltx_p">counts the number of colorings of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem26.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> inputs not allowing repetition of colors. Similarly, from the formula of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem26.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{S}_{U_{T}}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{S}_{U_{T}}(m)</annotation></semantics></math> in Example <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem25" title="Example 5.25. ‣ 5.3. Interpretation as the count of colorings ‣ 5. Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.25</span></a>,
it follows that</p>
<table id="S5.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathscr{S}^{\omega}_{U_{T}}(m)=(-1)^{n}&amp;\mathscr{S}_{U_{T}}(-m)=\begin{cases}\displaystyle{\binom{m}{n-2a}\cdot\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{\binom{m}{a}}{2}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)}&amp;\text{ if $a$ is even,}\\
\displaystyle{\binom{m}{n-2a}\cdot\binom{\binom{m}{a}}{2}}&amp;\text{ if $a$ is odd.}\end{cases}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mi>ω</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒮</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mi>a</mi><mtext> is even,</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mi>a</mi><mtext> is odd.</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathscr{S}^{\omega}_{U_{T}}(m)=(-1)^{n}&amp;\mathscr{S}_{U_{T}}(-m)=\begin{cases}\displaystyle{\binom{m}{n-2a}\cdot\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{\binom{m}{a}}{2}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)}&amp;\text{ if $a$ is even,}\\
\displaystyle{\binom{m}{n-2a}\cdot\binom{\binom{m}{a}}{2}}&amp;\text{ if $a$ is odd.}\end{cases}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem26.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This counts the number of proper colorings of the inputs of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem26.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S5.Thmtheorem26.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> colors.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6. </span>Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we study the asymptotic behavior and log-concavity of the polynomials <math id="S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{P}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{P}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> grows.
Since they are polynomials in two variables <math id="S6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we may consider several notions of log-concavity in Definition <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 2.1. ‣ 2. Two-dimensional log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We write</p>
<table id="S6.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{P}_{n,k}(m)=\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathscr{P}^{j}_{n,k}m^{j},\quad\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}(m)=\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathscr{Q}^{j}_{n,k}m^{j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{P}_{n,k}(m)=\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathscr{P}^{j}_{n,k}m^{j},\quad\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}(m)=\sum_{k\geq 0}\mathscr{Q}^{j}_{n,k}m^{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and provide asymptotic formulas for</p>
<ul id="S6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 6.1. ‣ 6.1. Asymptotic formulas ‣ 6. Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>) <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{P}_{n,k}(m_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{P}_{n,k}(m_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}(m_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}(m_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6.6. ‣ 6.1. Asymptotic formulas ‣ 6. Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.6</span></a>) <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{P}^{n-j}_{n,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{P}^{n-j}_{n,k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}^{n-j}_{n,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}^{n-j}_{n,k}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S6.p2.3" class="ltx_p">as <math id="S6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> grows with <math id="S6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,j</annotation></semantics></math> fixed, based on the combinatorial description in the previous section.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We then establish the asymptotic degree log-concavity at <math id="S6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=m_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=m_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (Corollary <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem9" title="Corollary 6.9. ‣ 6.2. Asymptotic log-concavity ‣ 6. Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.9</span></a>), the asymptotic degree ultra log-concavity in length <math id="S6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-j</annotation></semantics></math> (Corollary <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem10" title="Corollary 6.10. ‣ 6.2. Asymptotic log-concavity ‣ 6. Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.10</span></a>) and the asymptotic length log-concavity in degree <math id="S6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> (Corollary <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem11" title="Corollary 6.11. ‣ 6.2. Asymptotic log-concavity ‣ 6. Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.11</span></a>) for fixed <math id="S6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j,k</annotation></semantics></math>, by
using the asymptotic formulas.
The asymptotic formulas and the log-concavity results here generalize those in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In the remainder, we will use
the notation</p>
<table id="S6.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}=\frac{(k+1)^{k-1}}{k!}d_{k}=\frac{(k+1)^{k-2}}{k!}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}=\frac{(k+1)^{k-1}}{k!}d_{k}=\frac{(k+1)^{k-2}}{k!}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p4.2" class="ltx_p">These are the Cayley number <math id="S6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k+1)^{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k+1)^{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> of trees on <math id="S6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k+1</annotation></semantics></math> labeled vertices, divided by <math id="S6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k!</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k+1)!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k+1)!</annotation></semantics></math> respectively.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1. </span>Asymptotic formulas</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let us first find asymptotic formulas for
<math id="S6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{P}_{n,k}(m_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{P}_{n,k}(m_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}(m_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}(m_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6.1</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, as <math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> grows,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}&amp;\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}(m_{0})=\frac{c_{k}}{((k+1)m_{0}-1)!}n^{(k+1)m_{0}-1}+O(n^{(k+1)m_{0}-2}),\\
&amp;\mathscr{P}_{n,k}(m_{0})=\frac{d_{k}}{((k+1)m_{0}-1)!}n^{(k+1)m_{0}-1}+o(n^{(k+1)m_{0}-1}).\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}&amp;\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}(m_{0})=\frac{c_{k}}{((k+1)m_{0}-1)!}n^{(k+1)m_{0}-1}+O(n^{(k+1)m_{0}-2}),\\
&amp;\mathscr{P}_{n,k}(m_{0})=\frac{d_{k}}{((k+1)m_{0}-1)!}n^{(k+1)m_{0}-1}+o(n^{(k+1)m_{0}-1}).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 6.2</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem10" title="Lemma 3.10. ‣ 3.4. Characteristic polynomial of an 𝕊_𝑛-representation ‣ 3. Characteristic polynomials of symmetric functions and representations ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a> (2),</p>
<table id="S6.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{P}_{n,k}(1)=\mathrm{dim}\,H^{2k}(\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n})^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}(1)=\mathrm{dim}\,H^{2k}(\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n+1})^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>dim</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>dim</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{P}_{n,k}(1)=\mathrm{dim}\,H^{2k}(\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n})^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}(1)=\mathrm{dim}\,H^{2k}(\overline{{\cal M}}_{0,n+1})^{\mathbb{S}_{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence if we let <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math>,
Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 6.1. ‣ 6.1. Asymptotic formulas ‣ 6. Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a> recovers the asymptotic formula <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, Theorem 1.9]</cite>. Likewise, Corollary <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem9" title="Corollary 6.9. ‣ 6.2. Asymptotic log-concavity ‣ 6. Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.9</span></a> below with <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math> recovers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, Corollary 6.10]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">See §<a href="#S7.SS1" title="7.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ 7. Proofs of asymptotic formulas ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a> for a proof of Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 6.1. ‣ 6.1. Asymptotic formulas ‣ 6. Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>.
Here, we derive the formulas for <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}(m_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}(m_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math> as illustrative examples.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 6.3</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="S6.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There exists only one tree in <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{T}_{n,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{T}_{n,0}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the one described in Example <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem23" title="Example 5.23. ‣ 5.3. Interpretation as the count of colorings ‣ 5. Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.23</span></a> with weight 0 at the root. Thus,</p>
<table id="S6.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}_{n,0}(m_{0})=\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m_0}{n}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)=\binom{m_{0}+n-1}{m_{0}-1}=\frac{n^{m_{0}-1}}{(m_{0}-1)!}+O(n^{m_{0}-2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}_{n,0}(m_{0})=\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m_0}{n}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)=\binom{m_{0}+n-1}{m_{0}-1}=\frac{n^{m_{0}-1}}{(m_{0}-1)!}+O(n^{m_{0}-2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 6.4</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have two types of weighted rooted trees in <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{T}_{n,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{T}_{n,1}</annotation></semantics></math>, described in Examples <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem23" title="Example 5.23. ‣ 5.3. Interpretation as the count of colorings ‣ 5. Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.23</span></a> and <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem24" title="Example 5.24. ‣ 5.3. Interpretation as the count of colorings ‣ 5. Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.24</span></a> respectively.
Hence,</p>
<table id="S6.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}_{n,1}(m_{0})=\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m_0}{n}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)+\sum_{a=1}^{n-3}\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m_0}{a}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)\cdot\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m_0}{n-a}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}_{n,1}(m_{0})=\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m_0}{n}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)+\sum_{a=1}^{n-3}\left(\kern-3.00003pt\left(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m_0}{a}\right)\kern-3.00003pt\right)\cdot\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m_0}{n-a}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To obtain the asymptotic formula, notice that for <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S6.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\sum_{a=0}^{n}\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m_0}{a}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)\cdot\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m_0}{n-a}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)=\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{2m_0}{n}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)&amp;=\frac{n^{2m_{0}-1}}{(2m_{0}-1)!}+O(n^{2m_{0}-2}),\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0em;" width="0em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0em;" width="0em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0em;" width="0em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\sum_{a=0}^{n}\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m_0}{a}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)\cdot\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m_0}{n-a}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)=\Big(\kern-3.00003pt\Big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{2m_0}{n}\Big)\kern-3.00003pt\Big)&amp;=\frac{n^{2m_{0}-1}}{(2m_{0}-1)!}+O(n^{2m_{0}-2}),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">while <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\kern-3.00003pt\big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m_0}{n}\big)\kern-3.00003pt\big)=\frac{n^{m_{0}-1}}{(m_{0}-1)!}+O(n^{m_{0}-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.089em;" width="0.089em"><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\kern-3.00003pt\big(\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m_0}{n}\big)\kern-3.00003pt\big)=\frac{n^{m_{0}-1}}{(m_{0}-1)!}+O(n^{m_{0}-2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2m_{0}-1&gt;m_{0}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2m_{0}-1&gt;m_{0}-1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
