<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 6.5</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="S6.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The contribution of weighted rooted trees <math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{T}_{n,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{T}_{n,2}</annotation></semantics></math> with at most two vertices, to <math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}_{n,2}(m_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}_{n,2}(m_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, is</p>
<table id="S6.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
