<p id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Now we compute the contribution of <math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\mathscr{T}_{n,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\mathscr{T}_{n,2}</annotation></semantics></math> with three vertices. There are three types depending on the shape of trees without inputs and <math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Stab}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Stab</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Stab}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> so that</p>
