<div id="S6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We next present asymptotic formulas for the coefficients <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{P}^{n-j}_{n,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{P}^{n-j}_{n,k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}^{n-j}_{n,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}^{n-j}_{n,k}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{P}_{n,k}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{P}_{n,k}(m)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}(m)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> grows.
Recall that the <em id="S6.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">signless Stirling number of the first kind</em>, denoted by <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(n,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(n,j)</annotation></semantics></math>, is the number of elements <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\mathbb{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\mathbb{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> disjoint cycles.</p>
