<div id="S6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">From Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6.6. ‣ 6.1. Asymptotic formulas ‣ 6. Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.6</span></a>, we establish two asymptotic log-concavities of <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{P}_{n}(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{P}_{n}(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}_{n}(m,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}_{n}(m,t)</annotation></semantics></math>.
First, we show the asymptotic degree <em id="S6.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ultra</em> log-concavity in length <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-j</annotation></semantics></math> as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 6.10</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="S6.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for sufficiently large <math id="S6.Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

