<p id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p2.3" class="ltx_p">that sends <math id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sigma_{1},\sigma_{2},\sigma_{3};\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sigma_{1},\sigma_{2},\sigma_{3};\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}\tau\sigma_{3}\tau\sigma_{2}\tau\in\mathbb{S}_{I_{v_{1}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}\tau\sigma_{3}\tau\sigma_{2}\tau\in\mathbb{S}_{I_{v_{1}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For example, when <math id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=(1,5,9,4,2,6,7,8,3)\in\mathrm{Stab}_{\tau}(T)\subset\mathbb{S}_{I}=\mathbb{S}_{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=(1,5,9,4,2,6,7,8,3)\in\mathrm{Stab}_{\tau}(T)\subset\mathbb{S}_{I}=\mathbb{S}_{9}</annotation></semantics></math>, it can be written as <math id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=(\sigma_{1},\sigma_{2},\sigma_{3};\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=(\sigma_{1},\sigma_{2},\sigma_{3};\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}=(4,7)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}=(4,7)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{2}=(2,5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{2}=(2,5)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{3}=(3,6,9)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{3}=(3,6,9)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> as in (<a href="#S7.E9" title="In Example 7.9. ‣ 7.3. Quotient trees ‣ 7. Proofs of asymptotic formulas ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.9</span></a>). The image of <math id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> under (<a href="#S7.E10" title="In Example 7.9. ‣ 7.3. Quotient trees ‣ 7. Proofs of asymptotic formulas ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.10</span></a>) is the first projection of <math id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{3}=((1,4,7),(2,8,5),(3,9,6))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{3}=((1,4,7),(2,8,5),(3,9,6))</annotation></semantics></math>, which is <math id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,4,7)=\sigma_{1}\tau\sigma_{3}\tau\sigma_{2}\tau\in\mathbb{S}_{I_{v_{1}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,4,7)=\sigma_{1}\tau\sigma_{3}\tau\sigma_{2}\tau\in\mathbb{S}_{I_{v_{1}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem9.p4.1" class="ltx_p">One can also see that composing the third power map with the second or the third projection, rather than the first projection, yields maps, which are conjugate to each other.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Now we prove Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 7.8. ‣ 7.3. Quotient trees ‣ 7. Proofs of asymptotic formulas ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 7.8. ‣ 7.3. Quotient trees ‣ 7. Proofs of asymptotic formulas ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.8</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\mathrm{Stab}_{\tau}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\mathrm{Stab}_{\tau}(T)</annotation></semantics></math>, the length of <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the number of its orbits in <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> while the length of its image under (<a href="#S7.E6" title="In 7.3. Quotient trees ‣ 7. Proofs of asymptotic formulas ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.6</span></a>) is equal to the number of the orbits in <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{v_{1}}\sqcup\cdots\sqcup I_{v_{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>⊔</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊔</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{v_{1}}\sqcup\cdots\sqcup I_{v_{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since the <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-orbits in <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are in a bijective correspondence with the <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{d_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{d_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>-orbits in <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{v_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{v_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S7.SS3.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="S7.SS3.p12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(<a href="#S7.E6" title="In 7.3. Quotient trees ‣ 7. Proofs of asymptotic formulas ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.6</span></a>)</span> is length-preserving.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the second property, we will
endow an action of <math id="S7.SS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{\lambda(T/\tau)}=\prod_{j=1}^{p}\mathbb{S}_{I_{v_{j}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{\lambda(T/\tau)}=\prod_{j=1}^{p}\mathbb{S}_{I_{v_{j}}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S7.SS3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Stab}_{\tau}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Stab}_{\tau}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> so that (<a href="#S7.E6" title="In 7.3. Quotient trees ‣ 7. Proofs of asymptotic formulas ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.6</span></a>) is <math id="S7.SS3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{\lambda(T/\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{\lambda(T/\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant, with respect to the left multiplication on the target <math id="S7.SS3.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{\lambda(T/\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{\lambda(T/\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since the left multiplication is transitive,
this will imply that all the fibers are isomorphic to each other.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">By letting <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{j}=\lvert I_{v_{j}}\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{j}=\lvert I_{v_{j}}\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>, the map
<math id="S7.SS3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{v_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{v_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S7.E6" title="In 7.3. Quotient trees ‣ 7. Proofs of asymptotic formulas ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.6</span></a>)
is of the form</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}^{d_{j}}\rtimes\{\tau\}\hookrightarrow\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}^{d_{j}}\rtimes\mathbb{Z}/d\mathbb{Z}\longrightarrow\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}^{d_{j}}\xrightarrow{~pr_{1}~}\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub></mrow></mover><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}^{d_{j}}\rtimes\{\tau\}\hookrightarrow\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}^{d_{j}}\rtimes\mathbb{Z}/d\mathbb{Z}\longrightarrow\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}^{d_{j}}\xrightarrow{~pr_{1}~}\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS3.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">that sends <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma:=(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{d};\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma:=(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{d};\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}\in S_{n_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}\in S_{n_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=(1,\ldots,d)\in\mathbb{Z}/d\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=(1,\ldots,d)\in\mathbb{Z}/d\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> to</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\sigma^{d}&amp;=\left(\sigma_{1}\varphi_{\tau}(\sigma_{d})\cdots\varphi_{\tau^{d-1}}(\sigma_{2}),~\ldots,~\sigma_{d}\varphi_{\tau(\sigma_{d-1})}\cdots\varphi_{\tau^{d-1}}(\sigma_{1})~;~e\right)\\
&amp;=(\sigma_{1}\tau\sigma_{d}\tau\cdots\tau\sigma_{2}\tau,~\ldots,\sigma_{d}\tau\sigma_{d-1}\tau\cdots\tau\sigma_{1}\tau~;~e)\quad\in~\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}^{d_{j}}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>φ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>φ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>φ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.660em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.827em">;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>τ</mi><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>τ</mi><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0.827em">;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo rspace="1.000em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.938em">∈</mo><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\sigma^{d}&amp;=\left(\sigma_{1}\varphi_{\tau}(\sigma_{d})\cdots\varphi_{\tau^{d-1}}(\sigma_{2}),~\ldots,~\sigma_{d}\varphi_{\tau(\sigma_{d-1})}\cdots\varphi_{\tau^{d-1}}(\sigma_{1})~;~e\right)\\
&amp;=(\sigma_{1}\tau\sigma_{d}\tau\cdots\tau\sigma_{2}\tau,~\ldots,\sigma_{d}\tau\sigma_{d-1}\tau\cdots\tau\sigma_{1}\tau~;~e)\quad\in~\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}^{d_{j}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS3.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">and then to the first entry <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma_{1}\tau\sigma_{d}\tau\cdots\tau\sigma_{2}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>τ</mi><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}\tau\sigma_{d}\tau\cdots\tau\sigma_{2}\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, the <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th entry of <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma_{j}\varphi_{\tau}(\sigma_{\tau^{-1}(j)})\cdots\varphi_{\tau^{d-1}}(\sigma_{\tau^{-(d-1)}(j)})=\sigma_{j}\tau\sigma_{\tau^{-1}(j)}\tau\cdots\tau\sigma_{\tau^{-(d-1)}(j)}\tau\quad\in\mathbb{S}_{I_{v_{\tau(j)}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></msub></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}\varphi_{\tau}(\sigma_{\tau^{-1}(j)})\cdots\varphi_{\tau^{d-1}}(\sigma_{\tau^{-(d-1)}(j)})=\sigma_{j}\tau\sigma_{\tau^{-1}(j)}\tau\cdots\tau\sigma_{\tau^{-(d-1)}(j)}\tau\quad\in\mathbb{S}_{I_{v_{\tau(j)}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS3.p14.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p14.4.1" class="ltx_text">and we set <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{\tau}(a_{j}):=\tau a_{j}\tau^{-1}\in\mathbb{S}_{I_{v_{\tau(j)}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{\tau}(a_{j}):=\tau a_{j}\tau^{-1}\in\mathbb{S}_{I_{v_{\tau(j)}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, this map is <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{n_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant with respect to the left multiplication (only) on the first entry <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, (<a href="#S7.E6" title="In 7.3. Quotient trees ‣ 7. Proofs of asymptotic formulas ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.6</span></a>) is <math id="S7.SS3.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{j=1}^{p}\mathbb{S}_{I_{v_{j}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{j=1}^{p}\mathbb{S}_{I_{v_{j}}}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, the last inequality in the assertion follows from</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}_{\tau}^{\ell}(T)\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}_{e}^{\ell}(T/\tau)\rvert}=\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}_{\tau}(T)\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}_{e}(T/\tau)\rvert}=\frac{\lvert\mathbb{S}_{\lambda(T)}\rvert}{\lvert\mathbb{S}_{\lambda(T/\tau)}\rvert}\leq\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}(T)\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}(T/\tau)\rvert}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Stab</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Stab</mi><mi>e</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Stab</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Stab</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}_{\tau}^{\ell}(T)\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}_{e}^{\ell}(T/\tau)\rvert}=\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}_{\tau}(T)\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}_{e}(T/\tau)\rvert}=\frac{\lvert\mathbb{S}_{\lambda(T)}\rvert}{\lvert\mathbb{S}_{\lambda(T/\tau)}\rvert}\leq\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}(T)\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}(T/\tau)\rvert}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS3.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows from Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 7.1. ‣ 7.2. Stratifications of Stab(𝑇) ‣ 7. Proofs of asymptotic formulas ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
