<section id="S7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.4. </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6.6. ‣ 6.1. Asymptotic formulas ‣ 6. Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.6</span></a></h3>

<div id="S7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let us complete the proof. Recall that</p>
<table id="S7.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}_{n,\bar{T}}^{n-j}=\sum_{T\in F_{n}^{-1}(\bar{T})}\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}_{e}^{n-j}(T)\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}(T)\rvert}+\sum_{\tau\neq e\in\Aut(\bar{T})}\sum_{T\in F_{n}^{-1}(\bar{T})}\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}_{\tau}^{n-j}(T)\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}(T)\rvert}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Stab</mi><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Stab</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Stab</mi><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Stab</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}_{n,\bar{T}}^{n-j}=\sum_{T\in F_{n}^{-1}(\bar{T})}\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}_{e}^{n-j}(T)\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}(T)\rvert}+\sum_{\tau\neq e\in\Aut(\bar{T})}\sum_{T\in F_{n}^{-1}(\bar{T})}\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}_{\tau}^{n-j}(T)\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}(T)\rvert}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the asymptotic formula for the first summand in the right hand side is given in Proposition <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem6" title="Proposition 7.6. ‣ 7.2. Stratifications of Stab(𝑇) ‣ 7. Proofs of asymptotic formulas ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.6</span></a>.
When <math id="S7.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\neq e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\neq e</annotation></semantics></math>, by Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 7.8. ‣ 7.3. Quotient trees ‣ 7. Proofs of asymptotic formulas ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.8</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="S7.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\sum_{T\in F_{n}^{-1}(\bar{T})}\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}^{n-j}_{\tau}(T)\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}(T)\rvert}\leq\sum_{T\in F_{n}^{-1}(\bar{T})}\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}_{e}^{n-j}(T/\tau)\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}(T/\tau)\rvert}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Stab</mi><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Stab</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Stab</mi><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Stab</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\sum_{T\in F_{n}^{-1}(\bar{T})}\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}^{n-j}_{\tau}(T)\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}(T)\rvert}\leq\sum_{T\in F_{n}^{-1}(\bar{T})}\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}_{e}^{n-j}(T/\tau)\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}(T/\tau)\rvert}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Moreover, whenever the summand is nonzero on the right hand side, the number <math id="S7.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of inputs of <math id="S7.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T/\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T/\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S7.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert\lambda(T/\tau)\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert\lambda(T/\tau)\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>, thus greater than or equal to <math id="S7.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-j</annotation></semantics></math>.
This shows in particular that the right hand side is bounded above by</p>
<table id="S7.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n-j\leq n^{\prime}&lt;n}\sum_{T^{\prime}}\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}^{n^{\prime}-j^{\prime}}_{e}(T^{\prime})\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}(T^{\prime})\rvert}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Stab</mi><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Stab</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n-j\leq n^{\prime}&lt;n}\sum_{T^{\prime}}\frac{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}^{n^{\prime}-j^{\prime}}_{e}(T^{\prime})\rvert}{\lvert\mathrm{Stab}(T^{\prime})\rvert}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S7.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> runs over all the trees obtained by attaching <math id="S7.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> inputs to the vertices of <math id="S7.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{T}/\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{T}/\tau</annotation></semantics></math> in the way that they do not necessarily satisfy the valency conditions, and <math id="S7.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\prime}:=j-(n-n^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\prime}:=j-(n-n^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S7.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}-j^{\prime}=n-j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}-j^{\prime}=n-j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S7.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\neq e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\neq e</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the strict inequalities <math id="S7.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\prime}&lt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\prime}&lt;j</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert V(\bar{T}/\tau)\rvert&lt;\lvert V(\bar{T})\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert V(\bar{T}/\tau)\rvert&lt;\lvert V(\bar{T})\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence,
this is dominated
by the summand corresponding to <math id="S7.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=e</annotation></semantics></math> studied in Proposition <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem6" title="Proposition 7.6. ‣ 7.2. Stratifications of Stab(𝑇) ‣ 7. Proofs of asymptotic formulas ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.6</span></a>.
Combining all these results, we have</p>
<table id="S7.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7.11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}^{n-j}=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\bar{T}\in\mathscr{T}_{k}\end{subarray}}\mathscr{Q}_{n,\bar{T}}^{n-j}=c_{k}\cdot A_{j,k}(n)+O\left(\frac{k^{n}n^{2j}}{n!}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}^{n-j}=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\bar{T}\in\mathscr{T}_{k}\end{subarray}}\mathscr{Q}_{n,\bar{T}}^{n-j}=c_{k}\cdot A_{j,k}(n)+O\left(\frac{k^{n}n^{2j}}{n!}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This completes our proof of the asymptotic formula for <math id="S7.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{Q}_{n,k}</annotation></semantics></math> in Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6.6. ‣ 6.1. Asymptotic formulas ‣ 6. Asymptotic behavior and log-concavity ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We prove the case of <math id="S7.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{P}_{n,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{P}_{n,k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
First note that by definition,</p>
<table id="S7.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}n_{1}+n_{2}=n,\\
j_{1}+j_{2}=j\end{subarray}}A_{j_{1},k_{1}}(n_{1})\cdot A_{j_{2},k_{2}}(n_{2})=A_{j,k_{1}+k_{2}+1}(n)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}n_{1}+n_{2}=n,\\
j_{1}+j_{2}=j\end{subarray}}A_{j_{1},k_{1}}(n_{1})\cdot A_{j_{2},k_{2}}(n_{2})=A_{j,k_{1}+k_{2}+1}(n)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
