<p id="S7.SS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Now read the coefficients of <math id="S7.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{n-j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{n-j}</annotation></semantics></math> off (<a href="#S5.E3" title="In 5.2. Recursive formulas for characteristic polynomials ‣ 5. Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>),
multiply them by <math id="S7.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{n!}{(k+1)^{n-j}c(n,n-j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{n!}{(k+1)^{n-j}c(n,n-j)}</annotation></semantics></math> and take their limits as <math id="S7.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Then by (<a href="#S7.E11" title="In 7.4. Proof of Theorem ‣ 7. Proofs of asymptotic formulas ‣ Characteristic polynomial of ℳ̄_{0,𝑛} and log-concavity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.11</span></a>) and the above observation,</p>
